§ `Schedule 8 to the Order -- paragraph 1 of Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996 (personal allowances)`

-- Whether a regulation or a paragraph of the JSA Regulations 1996 applies to a person is for those Regulations (outside the
-- text), so each such test is a plain input. The heads that say "except where head (b) or (c) applies" or "head (a)
-- does not apply" are written out as they stand; the rule then takes the heads in the order the Schedule prints them,
-- first match (fork F-10).

§§ `Schedule 8 (1) -- single claimant`

-- out of text: Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 regs 57(2), 59 to 61, Sch 1 Part 3 para 13(1)(a); Jobseekers Act 1995 s 16: whether each applies is an input.
-- src:319 | (3) In Part 1 of Schedule 1 (applicable amounts: personal allowances)—
-- src:320 | (a) the sums specified in paragraph 1 shall be as set out in Schedule 8 to this Order; and
@ref art 26(3)(a) (src:319-320)
-- src:643 | | (1) Single claimant aged— | (1) |
-- src:644 | | (a) | except where head (b) or (c) of this sub-paragraph applies, less than 18; | (a) | £75.65; |
-- src:645 | | (b) | less than 18 who falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57 and who— | (b) | £75.65; |
-- src:646 | | (i) | is a person to whom regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies; or | |
-- src:647 | | (ii) | is the subject of a direction under section 16; | |
-- src:648 | | (c) | less than 18 who satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3; | (c) | £75.65; |
-- src:649 | | (d) | not less than 18 but less than 25; | (d) | £75.65; |
-- src:650 | | (e) | not less than 25. | (e) | £95.55. |
@ref Sch 8 (1) (src:643-650)
GIVEN `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 8 (1): the personal allowance of a single claimant` `the claimant's age` `the claimant falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the claimant` `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the claimant` `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `head (b)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (c)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (a)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18 AND `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 25 THEN JUST 75.65   -- (d)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 25 THEN JUST 95.55   -- (e)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `head (b)` MEANS
                `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18
            AND `the claimant falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57`
            AND (`regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the claimant` OR `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the claimant`)
        `head (c)` MEANS `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3`
        `head (a)` MEANS `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND (NOT `head (b)`) AND (NOT `head (c)`)

§§ `Schedule 8 (2) -- lone parent`

-- out of text: Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 regs 57(2), 59 to 61, Sch 1 Part 3 para 13(1)(a); Jobseekers Act 1995 s 16: whether each applies is an input.
-- src:651 | | (2) Lone parent aged— | (2) |
-- src:652 | | (a) | except where head (b) or (c) of this sub-paragraph applies, less than 18; | (a) | £75.65; |
-- src:653 | | (b) | less than 18 who falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57 and who— | (b) | £75.65; |
-- src:654 | | (i) | is a person to whom regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies; or | |
-- src:655 | | (ii) | is the subject of a direction under section 16; | |
-- src:656 | | (c) | less than 18 who satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3; | (c) | £75.65; |
-- src:657 | | (d) | not less than 18. | (d) | £95.55. |
@ref Sch 8 (2) (src:651-657)
GIVEN `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 8 (2): the personal allowance of a lone parent` `the claimant's age` `the claimant falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the claimant` `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the claimant` `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `head (b)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (c)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (a)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18 THEN JUST 95.55   -- (d)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `head (b)` MEANS
                `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18
            AND `the claimant falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57`
            AND (`regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the claimant` OR `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the claimant`)
        `head (c)` MEANS `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(1)(a) of Part 3`
        `head (a)` MEANS `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND (NOT `head (b)`) AND (NOT `head (c)`)

§§ `Schedule 8 (3) -- couple`

-- Each member of the couple is described by the facts the heads speak of. "The claimant" and "his partner" are the two
-- members; a head that says "one member" or "the other member" is tried both ways round.
DECLARE `a member of a couple claiming jobseeker's allowance` HAS
    `the member's age` IS A NUMBER
    `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation 59, 60 or 61 would apply to the member if they were not a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member is registered in accordance with regulation 62` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member falls within paragraph (2) of regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member would satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim, if they were not a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member satisfies the requirements of paragraph 13(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member is treated as responsible for a child` IS A BOOLEAN

-- out of text: Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 regs 57(2), 59 to 62, Sch 1 Part 3 para 13(1)(a); Jobseekers Act 1995 s 16; income support and income-related employment and support allowance entitlement: whether each applies to each member is an input.
-- (f): "a person under 18 who (i) is a person to whom regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies; or (ii) is the subject of a
-- direction under section 16; or (iii) satisfies requirements for entitlement to income support or who would do so if he
-- were not a member of a couple, other than the requirement to make a claim; or (iv) satisfies requirements for
-- entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance other than the requirement to make a claim"
@ref Sch 8 (3)(f) (src:680-684)
GIVEN `m` IS A `a member of a couple claiming jobseeker's allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 (3)(f): the member is a person under 18 who is described in (f)(i) to (iv)` `m` MEANS
        `m`'s `the member's age` LESS THAN 18
    AND (   `m`'s `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the member`
         OR `m`'s `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the member`
         OR `m`'s `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim`
         OR `m`'s `the member would satisfy the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim, if they were not a member of a couple`
         OR `m`'s `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim`)

-- out of text: Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 regs 57(2), 59 to 62, Sch 1 Part 3 para 13(1)(a); Jobseekers Act 1995 s 16; income support and income-related employment and support allowance entitlement: whether each applies to each member is an input.
-- (g) and (h): "a person under 18 (i) to whom none of the regulations 59 to 61 applies; or (ii) who is not the subject
-- of a direction under section 16; and (iii) does not satisfy requirements for entitlement to income support or an
-- income-related employment and support allowance disregarding the requirement to make a claim for it". Read as
-- printed, "(i) or (ii)" are alternatives and (iii) is additional (fork F-12). Because heads are tried in order and (f)
-- comes first, the reading cannot change an answer.
@ref Sch 8 (3)(g), (h) (src:685-692)
GIVEN `m` IS A `a member of a couple claiming jobseeker's allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 (3)(g), (h): the member is a person under 18 who is described in (i) to (iii)` `m` MEANS
        `m`'s `the member's age` LESS THAN 18
    AND (   (NOT `m`'s `regulation 59, 60 or 61 applies to the member`)
         OR (NOT `m`'s `a direction under section 16 is in force in respect of the member`))
    AND (NOT (   `m`'s `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim`
              OR `m`'s `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim`))

-- out of text: Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 regs 57(2), 59 to 62, Sch 1 Part 3 para 13(1)(a); Jobseekers Act 1995 s 16; income support and income-related employment and support allowance entitlement: whether each applies to each member is an input.
-- (a)(iii) and (vii): "satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support or an income-related employment and
-- support allowance other than the requirement to make a claim"
@ref Sch 8 (3)(a)(iii), (vii) (src:662-667)
GIVEN `m` IS A `a member of a couple claiming jobseeker's allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 (3)(a)(iii), (vii): the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support or an income-related employment and support allowance` `m` MEANS
       `m`'s `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to income support, other than the requirement to make a claim`
    OR `m`'s `the member satisfies the requirements for entitlement to an income-related employment and support allowance, other than the requirement to make a claim`

-- out of text: Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 1996 regs 57(2), 59 to 62, Sch 1 Part 3 para 13(1)(a); Jobseekers Act 1995 s 16; income support and income-related employment and support allowance entitlement: whether each applies to each member is an input.
-- src:658 | | (3) Couple— | (3) | |
