@ref Sch 9 (6) (src:707-711)
GIVEN `which condition` IS A `a condition of paragraph 15 of Part III of Schedule 1 to the JSA Regulations 1996`
      `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, or a partner of the claimant satisfies the condition by virtue of paragraph 15(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 9 (6): the severe disability premium` `which condition` `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, or a partner of the claimant satisfies the condition by virtue of paragraph 15(5)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which condition`
    WHEN `JSA paragraph 15(1) condition` THEN 86.05   -- (a)
    WHEN `JSA paragraph 15(2) condition` THEN
        IF `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, or a partner of the claimant satisfies the condition by virtue of paragraph 15(5)`
        THEN 86.05    -- (b)(i)
        ELSE 172.10   -- (b)(ii)

